    "body": "Adds ADR-008, which decides that we implement CSS selector parsing and matching ourselves in a new `renderer/css/` module.\n\nThis resolves the open question deferred from ADR-007:\n\n> **Recommendation:** implement selectors ourselves. This is deferred to a future ADR for the CSS engine, but noted here for context.\n\n## Scope of v1\n\n- Type, universal, class, id, and attribute selectors\n- Descendant, child, adjacent-sibling, general-sibling combinators\n- Selector lists (comma grouping)\n- Specificity per CSS 2.1: (a, b, c) triple, compared lexicographically\n\n## Deferred\n\n- Pseudo-classes, pseudo-elements, namespaces\n- CSS Selectors Level 4 extensions (`:has()`, `:is()`, `:where()`)\n- Performance optimizations (Bloom filters, style sharing)\n\n## Why\n\nUsing lexbor's selectors module would either require keeping lexbor's tree alive alongside our DOM (contradicting ADR-007) or reverse-converting on each match. We'd also need to parse selectors anyway to extract specificity, so the marginal savings of delegation are zero.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- New module `renderer/css/`\n- No new lexbor includes. ADR-007's isolation invariant still holds.\n\n## Next\n\nOnce ADR-008 is merged, the next issue will be \"Implement CSS selector matching per ADR-008.\"",
